@page
@model PortfolioManager.Web.Pages.Legal.TermsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of use";
}

<div class="col-lg-9">
    <h1 class="h2 pb-2 mb-3 border-bottom">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Version @LegalSettings.BuiltInVersion</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. About these terms</h2>
    <p>
        @Model.SiteName is run by @Model.OperatorWithAbn ("we", "us"). These terms apply when you create an account or
        use the site. By ticking "I agree" you accept them, together with our <a asp-page="/Legal/Privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        If you use the site for a business or for clients, you accept them for that business too.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. What the site is, and what it isn't</h2>
    <p>
        The site is software for keeping records of shares, cash, property and business transactions and for working out
        figures from those records, such as capital gains, income, franking credits, GST and ledger reports.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>It is not financial advice.</strong> Nothing on the site is a recommendation to buy, sell or hold
            anything, and it does not take your objectives, financial situation or needs into account.</li>
        <li><strong>It is not a tax agent service.</strong> Even if the people who run the site are registered tax or
            BAS agents, using the site does not make them your agent. They are not preparing or lodging anything for you
            unless you have a separate written agreement with them for that.</li>
        <li><strong>It is not legal or accounting advice.</strong> For advice about your own situation, see a qualified adviser.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>The figures depend on what you enter or import. You are responsible for checking that your records are complete and correct.</li>
        <li>Check figures before you lodge a return or a BAS, pay tax, or make a decision based on them, or have your own tax agent check them.</li>
        <li>Keep your password private, use a password you don't use elsewhere, and turn on two-factor sign-in.</li>
        <li>Only enter other people's information (for example, clients or tenants) if you are allowed to, and tell them how
            it will be used. If you run a practice on the site, you are responsible for your clients' consent.</li>
        <li>Don't enter tax file numbers. The site doesn't need them.</li>
        <li>Don't misuse the site: no attempts to get into other people's records, no harmful files, and no use that breaks the law.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">4. Calculations, prices and tax rules</h2>
    <p>
        We work to make the calculations right, but software can have errors, tax rules change, and some situations are
        handled in a simplified way. Share prices, exchange rates and other data come from outside providers and may be
        late, missing or wrong. Answers from the AI assistant can be wrong. Keep your own source documents (contract
        notes, statements, invoices), and download copies of your reports.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">5. The service</h2>
    <p>
        We may change, add or remove features, and the site may sometimes be unavailable, for example for maintenance.
        We back up the database regularly but cannot promise that no data will ever be lost. Where we can, we will
        give you notice before a change that takes away something you rely on.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. Other services you connect</h2>
    <p>
        If you connect another service (for example Navexa, Xero, MYOB or the AI assistant's provider), that service's
        own terms apply to it, and we are not responsible for what it does with your information or for its availability.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. Fees</h2>
    <p>
        The site is currently free. If we introduce fees, we will tell you first. Fees only apply once you agree to them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">8. Your rights under the Australian Consumer Law</h2>
    <p>
        Our services come with guarantees that cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law, including that they
        will be provided with due care and skill. Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or changes those guarantees
        or any other right you have that the law says cannot be excluded.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">9. Limits on our liability</h2>
    <p>As far as the law allows:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Where the law lets us limit our liability for failing to meet a consumer guarantee, our liability is limited
            to supplying the services again, or paying the cost of having them supplied again.</li>
        <li>We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss of profits, revenue or opportunity.</li>
        <li>We are not liable for loss caused by information you entered being wrong or incomplete, or by relying on figures
            you were asked to check without checking them.</li>
        <li>Our total liability to you for all claims about the site is limited to the fees you paid us in the 12 months
            before the claim arose, or AUD 100 if you have not paid us anything.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These limits don't apply to loss caused by our fraud or our deliberate wrongdoing.</p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">10. Security and data breaches</h2>
    <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect your information (see the <a asp-page="/Legal/Privacy">privacy policy</a>),
        but no website is completely secure. If a data breach is likely to cause you serious harm, we will tell you and
        the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner as the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme requires.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">11. Ending your use</h2>
    <p>
        You can stop using the site at any time and ask us to close your account and delete your records by emailing
        <partial name="_Contact" model="Model" />. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms or puts other
        users at risk; unless the risk is urgent, we will tell you first and let you download your records.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">12. Open-source software</h2>
    <p>
        The software that runs this site is open source under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3
        (<a href="@Model.Legal.SourceCodeUrl" rel="noopener">source code</a>). That licence covers the software itself
        and comes with no warranty. These terms cover the service we run with it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">13. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
        We may update these terms. When we do, we will show the new version and ask you to agree to it before you carry on
        using the site. If you don't agree, you can stop using the site and ask us to delete your records.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h5 mt-4">14. Law and contact</h2>
    <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of the Australian state or territory where @Model.Operator is based. Questions
        about these terms: <partial name="_Contact" model="Model" />.
    </p>
</div>
